title: 'SmartBear, on Cisco''s study of code review: people find most defects reviewing 200 to 400 lines at a time, under 500 an hour, for at most 60 to 90 minutes.'
pid: f064d0d0-efd9-46ff-8f2a-778d6301bf5a
body: |2-
  https://smartbear.com/learn/code-review/best-practices-for-peer-code-review/
  Summary, by the vendor whose tool was studied. Lightweight review
  "takes less than 20% the time of formal reviews and finds just as
  many bugs". Checklists help; authors who annotate their change find
  defects before the review. Took: the slice of some 400 lines; that it
  transfers to a model is my inference.
